# Citation metadata for the dataset.
#
# The Zenodo concept DOI is minted at the first deposit and is not known yet, so `doi` is absent
# from this file. The deposit steps are in docs/reports/README.md.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Kuzushiji Atlas, cite the release you used; every deposited version has its own DOI."
title: "Kuzushiji Atlas: a character-shape dataset of pre-modern Japanese writing"
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "mkpoli"
    website: "https://github.com/mkpoli"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mkpoli/kuzushiji-atlas"
url: "https://github.com/mkpoli/kuzushiji-atlas"
abstract: >-
  Kuzushiji Atlas is a character-shape dataset of pre-modern Japanese writing. One record is one
  graphic occurrence, in most cases one written character on a page image: its rectangle, the
  transcriber's string, a diplomatic reading, the Unicode code points including hentaigana, the 字母
  of kana forms, a variant key for kanji, and the document's production type, genre, register and
  date. Records come from open transcriptions aligned to open page images and from existing
  character-level datasets, with the licence of every image and text recorded per record. The
  annotations and the compilation are released under CC BY-SA 4.0; the code is MIT.
keywords:
  - kuzushiji
  - character-shape dataset
  - Japanese
  - hentaigana
  - IIIF
  - transcription
license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
